  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "Secretive marsh clans who survive by patience, memory, and sudden violence from the reeds.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Uthmori live on woven platforms above black water and remember kinship through pools, paths, and burial hummocks rather than through banners or walls. Their traditions are flexible in method but strict in loyalty: a stranger may be misled, stalked, or traded with depending on need, yet the clan's old rites are observed with stubborn care because forgetting them invites the swamp to swallow the living."
